  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Jom_W15_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Jom
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d01af24494056374182e13118c0585e2, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'Natural, adda met dagiti oras a kasapulam nga agsungbat iti ''no''
    wenno saan nga umanamong.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''saan'' ket kayatna a saoen
    ti ''no.''


    Mabalinmo nga agusar iti daytoy no kayatmo nga mangted iti negatibo
    a sungbat.


    Denggem a naimbag: saan.


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''saan''
    iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'Of course, sometimes you need to politely disagree or say ''no.''

    In
    Ilokano, ''saan'' means ''no.''

    You can use it when you want to give a negative
    response.

    Now, try saying ''saan'' yourself.'
